# W44-148 variant Z dct32x32 bisect (2026-05-21)

## Source

- Branch: main
- Parent commit: `b7d43d4b` (W44-147 photo audit Phase 1, investigate-only)
- Tool: `jxl-encoder/examples/w44_148_variant_z_dct32_bisect.rs`
- Reference encoder: cjxl `0.12.0` (libjxl build at `/home/lilith/work/jxl-efforts/libjxl/build/tools/cjxl`)
- Host: lilith (Ryzen 9 7950X, 128 GB)
- Date: 2026-05-21
- Target dir: `$HOME/work/zen/jxl-encoder-shared-target`

## Provenance

Per W44-147 Phase 1 finding: the dct32x32=1.20 in W44-96/98/99/100's variant
Z entropy_mul tables OVER-FIRES at broader photo d=5/6 corpus. The 1.20 value
was bisected against narrow W44-98/99 cells (4 cells × 1 distance);
broader-corpus measurement on the W44-147 audit reveals it's net-negative
SSIM2 on 1420710 d=6 (-2.13 ssim2) and 1531677 d=5/6 (-1.43 to -2.00 ssim2).

W44-148 bisects `dct32x32 ∈ {1.20 [current], 1.24, 1.28, 1.30, 1.34 [reference]}`
across all three variant Z tables (default Z, HC, LC) on 27 cells:
- DEFICIT_HC: 1420710 d=6 × e6/e7/e8/e9 (4)
- DEFICIT_LC: 1531677 d=5/6 × e7/e8 (4)
- SENTINEL_NOGATE: 1418519 d=5/6 × e7/e8/e9 (6) — gate doesn't fire, BYTE-IDENTICAL
- PROTECT_W98: 1420710 d=5 × e6/e7/e8/e9 (4)
- PROTECT_W99: 1531677 d=5/6 × e5/e6/e9 (5)
- BASELINE_W91: 1189261 e7 d=3/5 (2)
- BASELINE_NOGATE: 1025469 e7 d=3 (1)
- SCREEN_NOGATE: terminal e7 d=4 (1)

## Build

```
CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$HOME/work/zen/jxl-encoder-shared-target \
cargo run --release -p jxl-encoder \
    --features '__expert butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop parallel' \
    --example w44_148_variant_z_dct32_bisect
```

